      "q": "1. What are rights and why are they important? What are the bases on which claims to rights can be made?\nAnswer:\nRights are entitlements or justified claims that individuals, citizens, and human beings possess, recognised by society as legitimate and necessary for leading a life of respect and dignity. They are important because they provide the essential conditions for self-respect, dignity, well-being, and development of one\u2019s talents and abilities. The bases for claiming rights include the need for respect and dignity (such as the right to livelihood), necessity for well-being and development (like the right to education), and universal acceptance (applicable to all human beings equally). Rights are claimed based on collective agreement in society about what is essential for a good life and the recognition of equal value of all individuals.",
