      "q": "2. On what grounds are some rights considered to be universal in nature? Identify three rights which you consider universal. Give reasons.\nAnswer:\nRights are considered universal if they are applicable to all humans, regardless of nationality, race, caste, or gender, and are necessary for leading a life of dignity and self-respect. Three universal rights are:\nRight to Livelihood\n(it ensures economic independence and is essential to human dignity),\nRight to Freedom of Expression\n(vital for creativity and democratic participation), and\nRight to Education\n(develops reasoning, skills, and informed decision-making). These rights support personal and societal development and are accepted as fundamental by global communities, such as in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.",
