      "q": "6. Majority of people from the States of north India \u2013 Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar\u2014speak Hindi. If all these States are combined to form one State, would it be in tune with the idea of federalism? Give arguments.\nAnswer\nNo, merging these large and diverse states into one would contradict the core principles of federalism. Each state has its unique social, economic, and cultural context. Combining them would create an unmanageable administrative unit and would likely lead to resource imbalances, unequal development, and dissatisfaction among the people. Federalism is designed to respect regional diversity and promote balanced governance, which would not be possible in such a large, unified state.",
