      "q": "1. Which of the following do you feel are compatible with the idea of secularism? Give reasons.\n(a) Absence of domination of one religious group by another.\n(b) Recognition of a state religion.\n(c) Equal state support to all religions.\n(d) Mandatory prayers in schools.\n(e) Allowing separate educational institutions for any minority community.\n(f) Appointment of temple management bodies by the government.\n(g) Intervention of state to ensure entry of Dalits in temples.\nAnswer:\n(a) Absence of domination of one religious group by another:\nCompatible. Secularism stands for equality and opposes religious domination.\n(b) Recognition of a state religion:\nNot compatible. Secularism requires no official state religion.\n(c) Equal state support to all religions:\nCompatible, but complex. While in principle it promotes equality, state support must not lead to favoritism or dominance.\n(d) Mandatory prayers in schools:\nNot compatible. It violates religious freedom and secular values.\n(e) Allowing separate educational institutions for any minority community:\nCompatible. It enables protection of minority rights as per the Constitution.\n(f) Appointment of temple management bodies by the government:\nNot compatible if it leads to state interference in religious affairs without just cause. However, the state may intervene for reforms.\n(g) Intervention of state to ensure entry of Dalits in temples:\nCompatible. Secularism supports state intervention to end social/religious discrimination.",
